has a <title>","pass":true,"detail":""},{"id":"description","label":"Meta description present","pass":true,"detail":""},{"id":"charset","label":"Character encoding declared","pass":true,"detail":""},{"id":"lang","label":"Document language (lang) set","pass":true,"detail":"en"},{"id":"viewport","label":"Responsive viewport (zoom not disabled)","pass":true,"detail":"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0"},{"id":"open-graph","label":"Open Graph tags (5/6)","pass":true,"detail":""},{"id":"twitter-card","label":"Twitter card metadata","pass":true,"detail":""},{"id":"open-social","label":"Open social presence (Mastodon/Bluesky) linked","pass":false,"detail":""}],"passed":8,"total":11,"social":[],"og":{"title":"Center for Science, Management, Application/s, Regulation, and Training (SMART)","description":"The Center for Science, Management, Application/s, Regulation, and Training — Cyber SMART — combines computer science, related social and economic sciences, and behavioral and cognitive sciences to conduct cyber research for public and private sector organizations. With its analysis of current and emerging cyber issues, Cyber SMART is positioned to conduct collaborative research that is needed for the new era of cyber.   Cyber SMART’s approach includes working with those who have expertise in law, economics, management, neuroscience, and ethics. By coordinating, synthesizing, and holistically applying this multidisciplinary expertise to undertake cyber research and training, Cyber SMART is able to address all major considerations. This benefits industry, regulators, consumers, and society in general.     Cyber SMART’s members and affiliates include national and international corporations from the communications, banking, finance, insurance, retail, and logistics sectors as well as public sector organizations including regulatory agencies and law enforcement. These organizations face similar issues but from different perspectives, and that range of viewpoints informs Cyber SMART’s work. Cyber SMART’s multidisciplinary approach enables better understanding of cyber issues and opens new, underutilized avenues of inquiry. Its unique set of skills and expertise significantly increases the depth and breadth of research available to organizations and the research and education opportunities available to the workforce, academics, and students in a range of disciplines. It also informs policy, standards, and regulation.   Cyber SMART is uniquely positioned to conduct research that comprehensively addresses the consequences of increased digitization.  ","url":"/centers/center-for-science-management-applications-regulation-and-training-cyber-smart/","image":"/assets/images/twittercard.png","siteName":null,"type":"article"},"resilience":{"checks":[{"id":"pwa-https","label":"HTTPS (required for service workers)","status":"pass","evidence":"","exampleUrl":"https://iucrc.nsf.gov/centers/center-for-science-management-applications-regulation-and-training-cyber-smart/","why":"HTTPS is required for service workers and most install prompts."},{"id":"pwa-manifest","label":"Web app manifest declared","status":"fail","evidence":"","exampleUrl":"https://iucrc.nsf.gov/centers/center-for-science-management-applications-regulation-and-training-cyber-smart/","why":"A web app manifest is required for installability and controls how the app appears when launched."},{"id":"pwa-service-worker","label":"Service worker registered","status":"fail","evidence":"","exampleUrl":"https://iucrc.nsf.gov/centers/center-for-science-management-applications-regulation-and-training-cyber-smart/","why":"A service worker is what makes offline access, caching, and background sync possible."},{"id":"pwa-theme-color","label":"Theme color declared","status":"fail","evidence":"","exampleUrl":"https://iucrc.nsf.gov/centers/center-for-science-management-applications-regulation-and-training-cyber-smart/","why":"Theme color controls the browser chrome/status-bar color when the site is inst